Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               python3
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: flickos-recovery
Architecture: all
# btrfs-progs: the snapshots. On ext4 nothing runs, but the package is a
# Depends of flickos-desktop so installed systems get it (ADR-006).
# pkexec: putting back and the other changes from Settings (recovery-helper).
Depends: python3,
         btrfs-progs,
         pkexec,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: restore points of the whole FlickOS system
 Before every software change (apt, the Software and updates apps, automatic
 updates) a read-only btrfs snapshot of the system is taken: a restore point.
 One change gets one restore point, only the newest few are kept, and none is
 taken while the disk is nearly full. Nothing runs between changes.
 .
 It works only on FlickOS's btrfs layout (subvolumes @ and @snapshots), which
 new installs get. On ext4, and in the live session, it does nothing.
 .
 "flickos-recovery list" shows the restore points.
